    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (61.99) and **Cal Raleigh** (60.61) anchor the LawDog lineup as our strongest options. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive 13% boost via dynamic platoon splits against the right-handed Sonny Gray, and the favorable park factor provides the necessary ceiling to make him an elite play despite a lower spot in the batting order. Meanwhile, **Cal Raleigh** remains a high-floor selection; even with a conservative estimate for his position in the lineup, his ability to capitalize on projected wind-out conditions and the matchup against Roki Sasaki keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" category.\n\nThe bench decision process was dictated by our strict efficiency floor, most notably regarding **Braden Montgomery** (36.72). While his switch-hitting ability and high upside were considered, he fell short of the 40-point threshold required to displace starters like **Drew Gilbert** or **Jung Hoo Lee**. The primary risk today involves the heavy reliance on assumed lineups for **Cal Raleigh**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Lawrence Butler**; should those batting orders shift unfavorably, their calculated scores\u2014particularly those benefiting from top-of-the-order boosts like the 8% lift assigned to **Jonathan Aranda**\u2014could fluctuate significantly. We are keeping **Luis Arraez** in the leadoff spot against the left-handed Sears despite a platoon disadvantage, as his high-contact floor and the projected 10% order bonus outweigh the minor platoon dip. Monitor the official lineups closely, as the scarcity of stolen bases makes the utility of players like **Masyn Winn** and **JJ Bleday** vital in maintaining our position in the 5x5 standings.",
